F src/cli/guide.ts 810c5e3bc575 2026-09-30 warren.langeveldt/claude Guidance for people: ctx cards (fresh, stale and missing cards, for all files or those this branch changed) and ctx next (the one step to take, checked in priority order: no graph, broken graph or doctor failure, what the last session owes, the instruction block, changed files without cards, proposals and hygiene findings waiting for a person). Relies on cards.ts, doctor, hygiene, the recorder and git. The next skill runs its --json output and dispatches to the named skill, so step names must match skill names (init, status, cards, curate, done). Loaded lazily through commands.ts, so hooks never pay for it.
F src/cli/guide.test.ts 886a5a3c7ed1 2026-09-30 warren.langeveldt/claude End-to-end tests for ctx next and ctx cards on a temporary repository: each step next distinguishes, in its priority order, and that a project's [cards] exclude adds to the defaults. Runs nextStep with doctor off, since doctor inspects running processes.
F src/cli/commands.ts 0bae15eff75d 2026-09-30 warren.langeveldt/claude Lazy dispatch for lifecycle and runtime commands (init, ratify, pack, gate, hygiene, gc, retire, serve, overlay, bench, next, cards): each module loads only when its command runs, so the hook path, which runs on every tool call, never imports them. A new command that hooks don't need belongs here, not in main.ts.
F src/cli/main.ts 59a0b3420410 2026-09-30 warren.langeveldt/claude The ctx command line: argument parsing, usage text, and the commands hooks and agents call often (slice, hydrate, why, history, record, card, pending, coverage, doctor, install, hook, mcp). Rarer commands live behind commands.ts so this file stays cheap to load. Exports openFromArgs, needGraph and str for the lazily loaded modules; the usage text is what ctx help prints, so new commands are listed there.
F src/core/context.ts b1af886f83e9 2026-09-30 warren.langeveldt/claude Opens a repository: its root (the session's worktree when an agent works in a linked worktree of the project, else the project), its graph directory, and the effective config (defaults, then the graph's config.toml, then ~/.ctx/config.toml). Every setting has a default here. [cards] exclude adds to the default exclusions rather than replacing them; the defaults cover generated output, lockfiles, docs, configuration and dotfiles, which owe no card and need no read before an edit.
F src/init/instructions.ts 48462f93cfb0 2026-09-30 warren.langeveldt/claude The Context Graph block appended once to AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md, which agents re-read every turn: hydrate before reading, slice before shell edits, understand a file before editing it, write its card after, record owed decisions, and ctx next when unsure. Changing the text changes what every agent is told; the heading is how doctor and ctx next detect the block, so it must not change.
F src/core/context.ts 08a8a2edc564 2026-10-01 warren.langeveldt/claude Opens a repository: its root (the session's worktree when an agent works in a linked worktree of the project, else the project), its graph directory, and the effective config (defaults, then the graph's config.toml, then ~/.ctx/config.toml). Every setting has a default here. [cards] exclude adds to the default exclusions rather than replacing them; the defaults cover generated output, lockfiles, docs (Markdown and plain text), configuration and dotfiles, which owe no card and need no read before an edit.
F src/cli/doctor.ts c2bd33d37e4e 2026-10-01 warren.langeveldt/claude ctx doctor: one line per link in the chain that makes Context Graph work in a repository, each ok, warn or fail: the graph and its ratifiers, the ctx command on the PATH (with the install command when missing), the instruction block in AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md, the installed plugin version against the source, Claude Code processes started before the plugin was installed or updated (they never loaded its hooks), which sessions the hooks fired in during the last day, and whether ctx serve is up. ctx next and the status skill rely on a fail line meaning the setup is broken, so a fail must be something that stops Context Graph working, not a preference.
